.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1102 AM PDT Wed Sep 2 2026

Primarily VFR conditions with MVFR ceilings over the North Bay
that are expected to lift by 20z. A prefrontal band of light rain
will continue to move across the Bay Area into the early afternoon
with less than 0.10" of rainfall expected and minimal impacts. A
very deep marine layer (~5000ft) will be compressed somewhat
later today into late tonight, then deepen again by early Thursday
morning as a weak cold front moves across our area and the
troughing pattern persists.

Vicinity of SFO...Light rain in vicinity of the Bay Area terminals
should move east by 20z. VFR is expected to prevail through the
remainder of today and tonight with a chance of MVFR ceilings
developing after sunrise Thursday.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR through the remainder of today until
later tonight around midnight, when MVFR/IFR ceilings are expected
to develop. and persist through the remainder of the forecast
period. Confidence is higher this far south away from the more
prominent influence of the approaching cold front to the north.

